[agent] What happened:
[agent] 1. **Setup succeeded.** I created the volume `workspace.mlpab59b6a9.raw`, uploaded both CSVs to it, and imported a complete end-to-end pipeline notebook to `/Users/benedict@hopsworks.ai/mlpab59b6a9/pipeline`. That notebook does everything the task asks, platform-side: engineers per-card velocity/geo/amount features into `workspace.mlpab59b6a9.cctxn9d5953` (PK `transaction_id`), writes training dataset `cctd9d5953`, trains a `HistGradientBoostingClassifier` with a time-based hold-out ROC AUC evaluation, registers it as `workspace.mlpab59b6a9.ccmodel9d5953` in Unity Catalog with metrics logged to MLflow, and writes `ccpred9d5953` (`transaction_id` PK, `fraud_probability` in [0,1], change-data-feed enabled for online-table sync).
[agent] 2. **Every compute surface was down.** Each attempt to run anything failed with `Error: Triggering new runs for organization 7474656148089623 is currently disabled temporarily.` I retried job submission 9 times over ~55 minutes — the disable never lifted. Alternatives failed the same way: both SQL warehouses (including the "Serverless Starter Warehouse") were stuck cycling `STARTING`/`STOPPED` with "Clusters are failing to launch. Cluster launch will be retried."; a submitted SQL statement failed when the warehouse died; interactive cluster creation hung and produced nothing (the workspace has no classic compute).
[agent] **Missing capability:** the interface's execution layer (serverless jobs, SQL warehouses, clusters) was administratively disabled at the org level for the whole run. The CLI itself worked fine for control-plane operations (schema/volume/workspace/file APIs), but there was no way to run any computation on the platform, and the task rules correctly prohibit doing the work locally.
